.TH RUN 1 "November 2026" "Cyberus Linux Quest" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
run \- Cyberus Home Sweet Home challenge program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /challenge/run
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B /challenge/run
is a polite program that hands out instructions for claiming the Mission 02 flag,
but only if you ask nicely from inside a subdirectory of your home folder (\fB~/\fR\fIfolder\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print extra diagnostic status messages.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-please
Ask nicely to reveal instructions for claiming the flag.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dry\-run
Simulate execution without writing any files.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help and list supported options.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a directory inside your home folder, step inside it, and ask nicely:
.PP
.nf
.RS
mkdir ~/myfolder
cd ~/myfolder
/challenge/run --please
.RE
.fi
